  "scope": "Frozen descriptive comparison of five completed WR attempts with logged local native claims in the bounded5.1.19 window. This is not a population success-rate estimate.",
  "findings": [
    "The incomplete upright attempt and an accepted upright control have nearly identical positive capsule margin, jump age, flight time and network ping.",
    "Another accepted upright control has a smaller logged contact margin and nearly identical horizontal speed.",
    "Accepted controls also decelerate after the local claim and can leave contact before server confirmation. Early cancellation is not established as the server rejection cause.",
    "The planned continuous movement can be preserved only under its original validated deadline; any such change is a controller-contract correction, not a proven cure for rejected native claims."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Local BallTouched is a native client claim signal, not authoritative possession.",
    "Margin uses the logged current ball and hand/waist segment, not the exact native Reach packet or historical server state.",
    "The server rejection reason, exact server pose history, and exact native substep arguments are unavailable.",
    "The cases do not justify a universal margin, timing or radius threshold.",
    "No unlogged or future outcomes are imputed."
  ]
